<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Scipio Africanus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">236–183 BCE</span> · Also known as Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Publius Cornelius Scipio Africanus was the Roman general who defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthago-nova">Carthago Nova</a> in 209 BCE, won at Ilipa in 206 BCE, driving the Carthaginians from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, and in 204 BCE invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a> as ally. His victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> at Zama in 202 BCE ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/scipio-africanus.jpg" alt="Scipio Africanus" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: José Luiz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bust_of_Sulla_(loan_from_Ny_Carlsberg_Glyptotek)_-_Glyptothek_-_Munich_-_Germany_2017.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
